For my ideal evening discussion, I'd like to gather:

1. Alexander the Great - a Macedonian general and one of History's most prominent commanders;
2. Archimedes - an Ancient Greek polymath who is widely regarded as one of the greatest mathematicians and physicists of all time;
3. Leonardo da Vinci - an Italian Renaissance painter and polymath of the High Renaissance period, considered one of the greatest painters of all time;
4. Thomas Edison - a prolific American inventor, notable for his practical approach to invention, and a key figure in popularizing electric power and light for industry.

I would like to hear their thoughts on the role of reason and logic in modern life. They have unique contributions as thinkers, innovators, and influencers. We can discuss the benefits and drawbacks of human reliance on reason. We can explore the impact of logic in society and how it has shaped our world view.
